hrough structured data cabling, emphasizing the importance of robust data transmission capabilities. [Data: Entities (2292, 945), Relationships (3160)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Limitations of CAT 5e for High-Demand Applications\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While CAT 5e is a common standard, it is noted that it is not ideal for applications with high network demand. Compared to higher categories like CAT 6, CAT 5e has limitations that can affect performance in resource-intensive scenarios. For demanding network tasks, higher-grade cabling is generally recommended to ensure sufficient bandwidth and stability. [Data: Entities (392, 2322), Relationships (3217)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Residential Gateway/Distribution Device\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Residential Gateway/Distribution Device serves as the central point of distribution within a residential structured cabling architecture. This device typically operates within a star topology, acting as the hub where network connections converge and are distributed throughout the residence. Its role is integral to the organization and management of the home's network infrastructure. [Data: Entities (2297), Relationships (3167)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Cabling for CCTV Systems\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Closed-Circuit Television (CFTV) services are supported by structured cabling systems. Specifically, the cabling for CFTV in residential complexes often utilizes coaxial cable. This indicates a specialized application within the broader scope of structured cabling, catering to security and surveillance needs. [Data: Entities (2011), Relationships (3271)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 6.0,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is moderate, reflecting the essential role of these cabling standards in modern residential infrastructure and the potential disruptions if compromised.\"\n}